- P1 — Empty captured mutation output passes even `--require-executed`. `capture_run()` accepts a successful command producing zero bytes ([bin/coverloop:994](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:994)); unlike attached logs, it never rejects empty content ([bin/coverloop:1075](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1075)). `verify_capture()` then accepts the empty-file SHA-256 ([bin/coverloop:1515](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1515)), and strict execution mode passes it ([bin/coverloop:1551](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1551)). My pure-function reproduction returned `verify_empty_capture True` and a passing `require_executed_check`. Thus `--mutation pass --mutation-run true` can satisfy strict L3 mutation evidence without any guard-break transcript.

