- P2 — “GLM is always shown and never changes the verdict” is overstated. The promise appears at [docs/GATE.md:87](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/docs/GATE.md:87). An empty GLM object is hidden by `if g` at [bin/coverloop:1610](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1610); an invalid attached transcript prints only `transcript invalid`, omitting its status/count at [bin/coverloop:1612](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1612); malformed GLM fields reject the entire report through shared validation at [bin/coverloop:735](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:735). The ordinary valid `fail/7` case behaves correctly, but the unconditional documentation does not.

